<urn:beads-cache:finding:C4-FTQ-001> triage:id "C4-FTQ-001" ; triage:sprint "c-4" ; triage:severity "Important" ; triage:location "crates/bd-cache-daemon/src/readiness_tests/runtime_lifecycle.rs:193" ; triage:source "C4 QA1 actual parent-spawned reviewer fenced JSON" ; triage:status "open" ; triage:record "{\"evidence\": \"runtime_lifecycle.rs191 binds127.0.0.1:0;192 copies its assigned address;193 drops the sole listener;195 fixes that released address in endpoint_flag;197 asynchronously invokes start;198 begins serving probes. start() receives state_tx from stores at61-65/74-77; pinned sc-runtime0.1.1 builder.rs207-208 explicitly orders stores/routes before bind and binds only at356. Thus there is no continuous ownership across reservation and actual runtime bind. Source inspection proves the interleaving; no observed hosted failure is asserted.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-daemon/src/readiness_tests/runtime_lifecycle.rs\", \"id\": \"C4-FTQ-001\", \"issue\": \"The new public-runtime lifecycle test relinquishes its ephemeral TCP listener before the runtime binds the chosen address. Another concurrent listener can acquire that now-free address between drop(reservation) and the asynchronously started runtime bind. The test then fails its serving/cleanup handshake despite correct lifecycle behavior, or connects to the unrelated listener. The runtime stores handshake occurs before bind, so start() does not close this ownership gap.\", \"line\": 193, \"mechanism\": \"parallel_race\", \"recommendation\": \"Have the owning C2 test/runtime-fixture seam retain endpoint ownership through bind and report the actually bound endpoint, using a supported public upstream fixture or endpoint mechanism. Preserve real run_with_cleanup, actual signal and instance-lock assertions. Add a deterministic competing-bind negative that demonstrates the handoff is race-free; do not add bind retries, random-port loops, sleeps, timeout widening or a local framework fork.\", \"reviewer\": \"flaky-test-qa\", \"reviewer_records\": [{\"evidence\": \"runtime_lifecycle.rs191 binds127.0.0.1:0;192 copies its assigned address;193 drops the sole listener;195 fixes that released address in endpoint_flag;197 asynchronously invokes start;198 begins serving probes. start() receives state_tx from stores at61-65/74-77; pinned sc-runtime0.1.1 builder.rs207-208 explicitly orders stores/routes before bind and binds only at356. Thus there is no continuous ownership across reservation and actual runtime bind. Source inspection proves the interleaving; no observed hosted failure is asserted.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-daemon/src/readiness_tests/runtime_lifecycle.rs\", \"id\": \"C4-FTQ-001\", \"issue\": \"The new public-runtime lifecycle test relinquishes its ephemeral TCP listener before the runtime binds the chosen address. Another concurrent listener can acquire that now-free address between drop(reservation) and the asynchronously started runtime bind. The test then fails its serving/cleanup handshake despite correct lifecycle behavior, or connects to the unrelated listener. The runtime stores handshake occurs before bind, so start() does not close this ownership gap.\", \"line\": 193, \"mechanism\": \"parallel_race\", \"recommendation\": \"Have the owning C2 test/runtime-fixture seam retain endpoint ownership through bind and report the actually bound endpoint, using a supported public upstream fixture or endpoint mechanism. Preserve real run_with_cleanup, actual signal and instance-lock assertions. Add a deterministic competing-bind negative that demonstrates the handoff is race-free; do not add bind retries, random-port loops, sleeps, timeout widening or a local framework fork.\", \"reviewer\": \"flaky-test-qa\", \"severity\": \"important\", \"test\": \"canceled_read_keeps_runtime_instance_locked_through_real_signal_cleanup\"}], \"severity\": \"important\", \"test\": \"canceled_read_keeps_runtime_instance_locked_through_real_signal_cleanup\"}" .
